## Business Goals Constraints

- A campaign is an **immutable, versioned** node/edge graph that walks players through a journey: enrol, send outreach on a message rail, evaluate goals, route on the outcome.
- Versions are immutable so in-flight players always finish on the graph they enrolled in, and funnel history stays attributable to one definition. Cosmetic edits (message/offer ref) apply in place; anything that changes shape, timing or targeting forks a new version.
- Graphs are **CID-scoped**; `config.acceptedRealms` lists the PIDs a campaign may touch. One campaign can span realms.
- Publish refuses a send node whose rail reports itself definitely unconfigured, so an operator learns about missing credentials before players are enrolled, not after.
- The funnel answers "how far did each send get" per node: queued → sent → delivered → opened → clicked → converted, plus per-goal stages.

## Performance Constraints

- **Enrolment/dispatch**: batches of 500 from a per-CID token bucket that adapts to Mongo write latency. Code defaults: 500/s (burst 1000), 8 outstanding batches per worker; the runtime ships 3000/s (burst 6000), 64 batches.
- **Sends**: queued per CID at 500/s by default (the runtime ships 300/s), and paused while the rail's backlog for the CID would take longer than 300 s to drain. A player waits at most `SendQueueMaxWaitMs` (1 h default, 4 h shipped) to be handed to the rail, then routes `NotSent`.
- **Send retries**: a send that fails or is lost is queued again when its 120 s lease expires, up to 10 failures; the player then waits for the deadline and routes `NotSent`.
- **Funnel freshness**: writes buffer ~2 s, rollup seals every ~5 s behind a ~5 s safety margin, composed read cached ~3 s per `(cid, instance, live)`. Polling faster than ~3 s returns the same object.
- **`live=true`** adds a second query over the collection the event firehose writes to. Use `live=false` (sealed only, one query) on any view not watching a campaign in flight.
- **Pending window cap**: 30 s. When the rollup watermark trails further than that, the pending slice is not scanned and the read reports `lagging`.
- **Drain**: `MaxDrainDurationMs` defaults to 30 days, after which `WindingDown` escalates to `Halting`.
- **Publish preflight**: rail config check has a 5 s timeout; an unreachable rail is UNKNOWN and does not block.

## Usage Guide

### Auth

- All routes under **`/api/campaigns`**; CID/PID come from the request context, never the path.
- `[RequirePermission("Campaigns", Read|Write)]` → Admin, Developer, Tester (SuperAdmin always). Below Tester is 403.
- A **Write from a zone-scoped request requires Admin**.
- Headers: `Authorization: Bearer <operator token>`, scope header `{cid}.{pid|ZONE_*}`, `Content-Type: application/json`.
- Author identity comes from the token's `accountId`. `audit` is response-only; sending it is ignored.
- JSON is camelCase; enums are strings.

### Routes

| Route | Auth | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `POST /draft` | Write | Validate + save draft (no directory row; invisible to runtime) |
| `POST /publish` | Write | Publish in place or as a new version |
| `GET /` | Read | List, filter, page |
| `GET /{id}/{version}` | Read | Fetch graph (404 if none stored) |
| `GET /{id}/{version}/status` | Read | Lifecycle phase (404 for unpublished draft) |
| `GET /{id}/{version}/funnel?live=` | Read | Per-node funnel |
| `POST /{id}/{version}/deactivate` | Write | `{"mode":"Drain"\|"Hard"}` |
| `POST /{id}/{version}/archive` | Write | `Inactive → Archived` |
| `POST /{id}/{version}/reactivate` | Write | `Inactive → Launching` |
| `DELETE /{id}/{version}` | Write | Unpublished draft only (409 otherwise) |

### Draft and publish

- Validation failures are **HTTP 200 with `ok: false`**; check `ok` before trusting `version`. Only a malformed DTO or bad paging is 4xx.
- `/draft` writes nothing on failure — use it as the validation probe.
- Saves are **whole-document replace**. Never save a graph built from a partial read.
- `POST /publish` body: `{ "graph": {…}, "priorMode": "Drain" | "Hard" }` → `{ ok, version, isNewVersion, errors[], changes[] }`.
- `changes[]` = `{ kind: "Structural" | "Content", message, node, edge, field }`. Structural publishes a new version and cuts the prior one to `WindingDown` (Drain) or `Halting` (Hard).
- **Never write a default you did not mean** (`propertiesMode: "All"`, `target: "Value"`, empty `values`/`properties`, null `withinMs`/`observePid`). The classifier compares serialized bytes, so it forks a new version over nothing.

### List

All params optional, AND-ed, offset paging: `campaignId`, `name` (case-insensitive prefix), `phase` (repeatable), `createdBy`/`publishedBy` (account id or email), `tag`, `realm` (PID in `acceptedRealms`), `createdAfter/Before`, `publishedAfter/Before` (ISO-8601), `sort` (`CreatedAt` default, `PublishedAt`, `LastUpdatedAt`, `Name`, `CampaignId`), `descending` (default `true`), `skip` (≥ 0), `limit` (1–200, default 50). Out-of-range values are 400, not clamped.

Response `{ records[], total, skip, limit }`. One row per **(campaign, version)**, drafts included. Current version = max `version` per `campaignId`. Omitting `realm` returns every realm in the CID.

### Lifecycle

```
Draft ──publish──▶ Launching ──(system)──▶ Active
                       │                     │
                       ├─ deactivate Drain ─▶ WindingDown ─┐
                       └─ deactivate Hard ──▶ Halting ─────┤ (system: drained / MaxDrainDuration)
                                                           ▼
                                   Inactive ──archive──▶ Archived
                                       └──reactivate──▶ Launching
```

- Enrolment only in `Launching`/`Active`; in-flight players progress through `WindingDown`, stop at `Halting`.
- Commands are async desired-state writes: **poll `/status`** after each.
- Commands return 200 (empty) or **409 when inapplicable** — expected, not a failure. Re-issuing an applied command returns 200.

### Funnel

```json
{ "campaignId": "cmp-7f3a91c2", "version": 1,
  "nodes": [ { "node": "send-1-1-1", "stages": {
      "beam_sent":   { "sealed": 118, "pending": 2, "lagging": false },
      "beam_goal_purchase@DE_1234": { "sealed": 9, "pending": 0, "lagging": false },
      "beam_met_purchase@DE_1234":  { "sealed": 7, "pending": 0, "lagging": false } } } ] }
```

| key | meaning |
|---|---|
| `beam_queued` | campaign handed the send to the rail |
| `beam_sent` | rail acked |
| `beam_delivered` · `beam_opened` · `beam_clicked` | engagement |
| `beam_converted` | player met an objective |
| `beam_goal_{label}` | player **fired** one of the goal's leaves |
| `beam_met_{label}` | player **met** the objective |

- Each stage is `{sealed, pending, lagging}`. Display `sealed + pending`.
- `lagging: true` → floor, not total; a lagging `0` is *unknown*, never render it as zero. Applied campaign-wide.
- `live=false` → `pending: 0` means *not asked*, not *nothing outstanding*.
- `beam_goal_*` ≠ `beam_met_*` for `AllOf`/`AnyOf`; never merge or label the first "conversions".
- Every graph node reports its full stage list; all-zero = nothing sent yet, **404 = no such version**.
- `beam_` is reserved; authored event names inside it fail publish with `ReservedEventName`.
- 64-bit values arrive as `bigint | string`; never `Number()` an id.

### Graph DTO

```
CampaignGraphDto { campaignId, version, config, nodes[], edges[], audit? }
config: { name, options[], acceptedRealms[], tags[], maxDrainDurationMs? }
        options ∈ "AllowSimultaneousLanes" | "AllowCidLevelSegments"
node:   { id, lane?, body, outcomes[{ key, timing: "Immediate"|"Delayed" }], incomingDecorators[], outgoingDecorators[] }
body:   { kind: "Entry"|"Segment"|"Conditional"|"Schedule"|"Send", entry?|segment?|conditional?|schedule?|send?, customProperties? }
  entry       { trigger: { kind: "AutoSegment"|"Event"|"Inaction", segment?, event?, windowMs? },
                requalify: { kind: "Never"|"Immediately"|"After", cooldownMs? } }
  segment     { segment, evaluationWindowMs? }
  conditional { expression: Condition, maxWaitMs? }
  schedule    { kind: "DelayFor"|"SendNow"|"AtDateTime", delayMs?, when? }
  send        { railFederationId, targetPid, message, goals[], maxWaitMs, deliveryMaxWaitMs?,
                campaignOffers?[], campaignOfferGroups?[] }
    offer     { entryId, offerId, federationId, label?, invalidatesEntryIds?[], condition?, extraData? }
      condition { payload (segmentation rule, flat REST encoding), lockedMessage? }
    group     { id, memberEntryIds[], mode: "All"|"Exclusive", invalidation: "None"|"Single"|"Group", label? }
edge:   { id, from, outcome, to, decorators[] }
```

- Every recipient of a send is granted every offer of the node, on the store federation named by `federationId`. A `condition` is a gate, not a filter: the offer reports itself unavailable until the player qualifies.
- A group's `mode`: `All` = members stack, `Exclusive` = members are alternatives. `invalidation` = what a purchase forfeits: `None` (the only value valid for `All`), `Single` (each member forfeits the entries in its `invalidatesEntryIds`), `Group` (buying any member forfeits every other member).
- Limits per graph: 500 nodes, 2000 edges; per send node: 32 goals, 48 offers, 48 offer groups.

- `kind` must match the populated branch, else `400 InvalidCampaignGraph`.
- `maxWaitMs` = conversion window from the rail's Sent ack; `deliveryMaxWaitMs` = delivery ceiling (default 15 min). Both > 0. Goal `timerMs` ≤ `maxWaitMs` (null inherits).
- Every PID referenced (incl. per-leaf `observePid`) must be in `config.acceptedRealms`.
- Goal labels become Mongo field names: no `.`, no leading `$`, unique per node. Derive from a stable id (labels key `beam_met_{label}`; renaming orphans history). Convention: `{goalId}@{pid}`, bare `{goalId}` for cross-scope `AllOf`.

### Validation errors

`{ code, message, node?, edge?, goalLabel? }` inside a 200. Read the coordinates; never parse `message`.

- Shape: `DuplicateNodeId`, `DuplicateEdgeId`, `EdgeReferencesUnknownNode`, `EdgeOutcomeNotDeclared`, `GraphHasCycle`, `NodeUnreachable`, `LaneHasMultipleAutoSegmentEntries`
- Targeting: `SendTargetPidRequired`, `GoalObservePidRequired`, `PidNotInAcceptedRealms`, `CidLevelSegmentNotAllowed`
- Goals: `GoalPredicateEmpty`, `GoalAbsenceWindowInvalid`, `GoalTimerExceedsMaxWait`, `GoalPropertyBoundInvalid`, `DuplicateGoalLabel`, `InvalidGoalLabel`, `ReservedEventName`
- Windows: `SendDeliveryWindowInvalid`, `SendConversionWindowInvalid`
- Offers: `OfferEntryIdDuplicate`, `OfferReferenceIncomplete`, `OfferGroupMemberUnknown`, `OfferGroupTooSmall`, `OfferGroupModeConflictsWithInvalidation`, `OfferGroupInvalidationUnconfigured`, `OfferInMultipleGroups`, `OfferSelfInvalidation`, `OfferForfeitsAcrossFederations`, `OfferConditionRuleInvalid`
- Size: `GraphTooLarge`, `SendNodeTooLarge`, `PropertyTooLarge`
- Publish only: `RailNotConfigured` (names every missing key), `OfferFederationNotRegistered`
- HTTP: `400 InvalidCampaignGraph`, `400 InvalidCampaignPageLimit`/`InvalidCampaignPageSkip`, 401, 403, 404, 409

### End to end

```http
GET  /api/campaigns?realm=DE_1234&phase=Active&limit=50
POST /api/campaigns/draft    { …CampaignGraphDto… }               → { "ok": true, "errors": [] }
POST /api/campaigns/publish  { "graph": {…}, "priorMode": "Drain" } → { "ok": true, "version": 1, "isNewVersion": true }
GET  /api/campaigns/cmp-7f3a91c2/1/status                         → poll "Launching" → "Active"
GET  /api/campaigns/cmp-7f3a91c2/1/funnel
POST /api/campaigns/cmp-7f3a91c2/1/deactivate { "mode": "Drain" }
GET  /api/campaigns/cmp-7f3a91c2/1/status                         → poll until "Inactive"
POST /api/campaigns/cmp-7f3a91c2/1/archive
```
